<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 291 0 R
/E (Hart, Nilsson, and Raphael introduced the A* algorithm, providing a formal and systematic approach for determining minimum-cost paths using heuristic guidance. Their work combines actual path cost with an estimated cost to the goal, enabling efficient search while ensuring optimality under Hart, Nilsson, and Raphael introduced a foundational work that provides a formal basis for the heuristic determination of minimum-cost paths, leading to the development of the well-known A* search algorithm. This research establishes a systematic approach for pathfinding by combining the actual cost from the start node with a heuristic estimate of the remaining cost to reach the goal. The authors demonstrate how admissible and consistent heuristics ensure optimality and efficiency in path computation. By guiding the search toward the most promising paths, the algorithm significantly reduces computational complexity compared to uninformed search methods.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
