<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 292 0 R
/E (Alzantot and Youssef proposed CrowdInside, a novel system for the automatic construction of indoor floor plans using data collected from crowd-sourced smartphone sensors. The system leverages inertial sensors, such as accelerometers and gyroscopes, to track user movement and infer indoor structural features including corridors, rooms, and intersections. By aggregating data from multiple users, CrowdInside is able to generate accurate indoor maps without requiring pre-existing floor plans or manual surveying. This approach reduces the cost and effort associated with creating indoor layouts, making it scalable for large buildings. However, the system relies heavily on continuous sensor data collection and user participation, which may introduce noise and accuracy issues. In the context of indoor navigation, this work highlights an alternative method for obtaining indoor spatial representations. While effective for map generation, it differs from grid-based, static-map approaches that prioritize simplicity and low infrastructure requirements.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
