816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 293 0 R
/E (Ranoliya, Raghuwanshi, and Singh presented a chatbot system designed to handle university-related frequently asked questions, aiming to improve access to administrative and academic information. The proposed chatbot uses natural language processing techniques to understand user queries and provide relevant responses related to admissions, courses, examinations, schedules, and general campus information. By automating responses to repetitive queries, the system reduces the workload on administrative staff and improves response time for students. The study demonstrates how conversational interfaces can enhance user interaction and information retrieval in educational institutions. However, the chatbot is primarily limited to textual information delivery and does not support spatial navigation or location-based assistance. Despite this limitation, the work highlights the effectiveness of chatbots in academic environments and establishes the importance of natural language interaction for user engagement. This research motivates the integration of chatbot technology with indoor navigation systems, where conversational interfaces can be extended beyond information retrieval to guide users spatially within campus buildings.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
